lifeos-nix patch f-verification-rule8 — add rule 8 (falsifier fidelity) to the verification doctrine

ORDER
  Applies AFTER f-incidents-retire. Both touch algorithm-tab.ts; this one edits the
  Verification role string, the other removes the Incidents entry a few lines below, so
  the hunks are generated against the already-patched tree and must stay in that order
  in default.nix.

PROBLEM
  The seven verification rules all ask the same shape of question: is this the right
  probe, on the right path, at the right time? None asks whether the probe can go red at
  all. A grep of the doctrine for mutation / tautology / by-construction returns nothing.

  Found live (stroskar revenue layer, 2026-09-01, eight review rounds): three tests could
  not fail on any plausible single change to production code. One looped over the same
  constant the code builds its SQL clause from, and stayed green when that constant was
  mutated into literally the bug it exists to prevent. One asserted a fact about a config
  file it never read. Four negative assertions passed against an EMPTY parse result, i.e.
  against total failure of the reader, because all() over nothing is True.

  The mirror error appeared in the same session and is why the rule names its method: a
  reviewer argued from reading that a central balance test was a tautology, the argument
  was accepted without a mutation, written into a decision record and a commit message,
  and reported twice — then falsified by a single mutation that broke the test in both
  parametrisations. A confident structural argument about a test sounds like it has
  already been verified, which is exactly why it skips verification. Every error of this
  class in that session, in both directions, came from reading.

  Contributing factor: the Hardening skill already performs mutation testing. Nothing in
  doctrine said WHEN reaching for it becomes obligatory, so it was never reached for.

FIX (3 files)
  Verification.md   — rule 8, section heading six->eight... seven->eight, version 2.2.1
                      -> 2.3.0. Rules 1-7 untouched.
  SYSTEM_PROMPT.md  — the resident pointer: seven -> eight, falsifier fidelity named in
                      the by-name list, and the load-trigger list gains "when judging
                      whether a green test is evidence".
  algorithm-tab.ts  — the Pulse doc-map role string for Verification.md said "six" and
                      omitted cache fidelity (stale upstream by one before this change);
                      now says eight and lists all of them. The trailing "Cites incidents
                      by INC-ID." is dropped with the retired surface.

  No hook, tool or test reads the rule text, so nothing executable changes. The rule is
  doctrine the model follows, not a gate — deliberately: a gate that tried to detect an
  unfailable test would have to run the mutation itself, which is the Hardening skill's
  job and is invoked per-run, not per-edit.

